    "conventions": "Most Indonesians have no inherited family name. Many Javanese, especially older people, use a single name (Sukarni, Slamet), and others carry two or three personal names where the last one is not passed on: Budi Santoso's children will not be Santosos. The family list for Javanese, Sundanese and Muslim Jakartan names therefore holds common second names, with family_f giving the ones women usually carry (Lestari, Rahayu). Batak people do carry a clan name (marga) such as Siregar or Simanjuntak, and Batak women write it after boru (br.). Chinese Indonesians mostly use Indonesian-sounding family names like Wijaya, Gunawan or Halim. People are addressed by first name with Pak, Bu, Mas, Mbak or Bang.",
